<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>The Battle of Mitú, 1995</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;This scenario assumes that violence from the FARC conflict with Colombia has spilled over into Brazil.&amp;nbsp; Brazilian citizens have been kidnapped and killed.&amp;nbsp; Among other crimes, FARC is blamed for the brutal murders of a Brazilian police captain and his family.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;FARC currently occupies the Colombian town of&amp;nbsp;Mitú, close to the Colombia-Brazilian border.&amp;nbsp; Brazil has decided to raid this FARC stronghold.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;This scenario presumes a "best case scenario" for the FARC guerillas, who were believed to have captured a few 81-mm mortars from the Colombian army and who were also believed to have gained possession of&amp;nbsp;a few&amp;nbsp;man-portable surface-to-air missiles.&amp;nbsp; It also assumes FARC was successful in negotiating the purchase of additional heavy weapons from arms dealers.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;-------------------------------------------------------&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;A delta template .ini file has been included in the .zip file to assist in updating the scenario to any future versions of the database.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;Scenario Author: Mark Gellis&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
